Near miss for comment_text_after_terminator: a multi-line comment ends,
then a blank line, then a prose-shaped line. The paragraph break means
the comment ended deliberately, so the orphaned-prose signal is
suppressed (issue #6). The stranded words are still not SSL and remain
unexpected_token's to report.
-- input.ssl --
/* a multi-line note
that spans two lines;

these words follow a paragraph break;
:DECLARE nCount;
nCount := 0;
-- format --
/* a multi-line note
that spans two lines;

these words follow a paragraph break;
:DECLARE nCount;
nCount := 0;
-- diagnostics --
4:7-4:12 error unexpected_token: Unexpected identifier 'words' - expected an operator or ';'
